Bugzilla
========

Bugzilla is free and open source web-based bug-tracking software that is
developed by an active group of volunteers in the Mozilla community, and used
by thousands of projects and companies around the world. It can be installed on
Linux and other flavors of Unix, Windows or Mac OS X.

Documentation
=============

Bugzilla's comprehensive documentation, including installation instructions,
can be found here:
http://www.bugzilla.org/docs/

Docker Quick Start
==================

If you have Docker installed and just want to take a quick look around Bugzilla
you can cd into the bugzilla directory (same directory containing this README)
and type `docker compose up`. The URL to access and the username and password
for the default admin account will be shown on the console once it finishes
setting it up.

If checksetup.pl stops in Docker because UTF-8 conversion requires an
interactive confirmation, you can explicitly allow that conversion with:

	BZ_ALLOW_UNSAFE_UTF8_CONVERSION=1 docker compose up

Only do this if you understand the warning and have a backup of your data.

Upgrading the Docker database
-----------------------------

WARNING: An existing database must be upgraded when moving to the MariaDB 12.3
image. Automatic upgrade is disabled by default. Starting the server without
completing the upgrade can leave system tables or application tables
incompatible and cause errors or unexpected behavior.

Before starting MariaDB 12.3 against an existing volume:

1. Back up the entire database and verify that the backup can be restored.
2. Stop Bugzilla and shut down the existing MariaDB server cleanly. MariaDB
   12.3 cannot upgrade a 10.6 data directory that was not shut down cleanly.
3. Review the MariaDB upgrade instructions, including incompatible changes
   between your current and target versions:
   https://mariadb.com/docs/server/server-management/install-and-upgrade-mariadb/upgrading/

Starting the new server can change data files, and upgrading can change system
tables and affect downgrade options. The image's automatic system-table backup
is not a complete backup of the Bugzilla database.

Start only the database service and choose one of these upgrade methods before
starting Bugzilla:

Automatic system-table upgrade:

    MARIADB_AUTO_UPGRADE=1 docker compose up -d --build bugzilla5.db
    docker compose logs bugzilla5.db

Wait until the logs show that mariadb-upgrade finished successfully and the
server is ready for connections. The image's automatic upgrade updates system
tables but does not check application tables. Run the following command to
check and upgrade all tables:

    docker compose exec --user mysql bugzilla5.db mariadb-upgrade --force -u root -p

Enter the database root password when prompted.

Manual upgrade:

With automatic upgrade disabled, start the database service:

    docker compose up -d --build bugzilla5.db

Once the database is ready, run:

    docker compose exec --user mysql bugzilla5.db mariadb-upgrade -u root -p

Enter the database root password when prompted. Check the command output for
errors. If the server cannot start or the upgrade fails, consult the MariaDB
upgrade documentation before proceeding.

After the upgrade completes, verify the database and start Bugzilla:

    docker compose up -d --build

The MariaDB 12.3 database container provides the mariadb client rather than
mysql. For example, use docker compose exec bugzilla5.db mariadb for
interactive database access.

Reporting Bugs
==============

Report bugs here:
https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Bugzilla

(Please do not file test bugs in this installation of Bugzilla.)

Mailing Lists
=============

Development:
https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/forums/#dev-apps-bugzilla

Support:
https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/forums/#support-bugzilla

IRC
===

You can often find Bugzilla developers on IRC:
irc://irc.mozilla.org/bugzilla

